BT /F2 12 Tf 56 684 Td (Summary) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 664 Td (SEV3 incident on April 22, 2026 affecting fraud-scorer and payments-api. The fraud-scorer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 650 Td (feature store fell behind with a lag of 12 minutes, causing payment approvals to wait on fresh) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 636 Td (features and become slower. Marco Bellini investigated. The issue was resolved by restarting) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 622 Td (the feature consumer.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 56 600 Td (Impact) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 580 Td (Payment approval latency increased by 3 seconds slower during the incident window. Merchants) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 566 Td (experienced slower payment processing as the fraud-scorer service waited for feature store) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 552 Td (updates. See STS-403 for real-time status updates during the incident.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 56 530 Td (Timeline) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 510 Td (- 14:32 UTC: Monitoring alert triggered for feature store lag) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 490 Td (- 14:35 UTC: Incident commander notified; Marco Bellini began investigation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 470 Td (- 14:41 UTC: Root cause identified as feature consumer process stalled) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 450 Td (- 14:43 UTC: Feature consumer restarted) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 430 Td (- 14:45 UTC: Feature store lag returned to normal; payment approval latency normalized) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 56 408 Td (Root cause) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 388 Td (The fraud-scorer feature store consumer process stopped consuming messages from the upstream) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 374 Td (data pipeline, causing the feature store to fall behind by 12 minutes. This lag forced the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 360 Td (payments-api to wait for fresh features during fraud scoring, adding latency to payment) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 346 Td (approvals.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 56 324 Td (Resolution) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 304 Td (The feature consumer was restarted, which resumed normal message consumption and cleared the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 290 Td (accumulated lag. Payment approval latency returned to baseline within 2 minutes of restart.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 56 268 Td (Follow-up actions) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 248 Td (- Implement automated alerting for feature store lag as described in CHG-1080) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 228 Td (- Review RB-12 for standard procedures to follow during future feature store lag incidents) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 208 Td (- Investigate why the feature consumer process stalled and implement safeguards to prevent) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 194 Td (  recurrence) Tj ET
